  "notes": [
    "CAMPAIGN.md §10.1 / §12.2 '6-1'..'6-6'. 6-1 reuses ch1's towers (E1a2 176-464, E1a0 928-1312) five chapters later in storm (user question 4 default); their 48-px lanes get the same floor-art walk patches as in ch1. 6-1 is re-ordered as E1a2, E1a2 flip, E1a0, E1a0 flip so the two sources meet once (under a pier) and every other join is a mirror join.",
    "E8a1 past 2992 (CAMPAIGN 6-4, 6-6) is not used: the original camera falls there during a fade (segment 0x09 at 3008), its terrain is type 0 in every row and its scroll2 is empty from X 3100, so a lane there stands on nothing. 6-4's dam halls are E6a0 1216-1728 (mirror pair) and the dam control hall E7a3 880-1264 with its mirror (the E7a3 riser and consoles; ch5 uses E7a3 0-512 only, and the Slisaur monitor wall 1264+ is left out); 6-6's spillway is the E8a1 sluice basin 1504-1664 and its mirror (lane probed live, work/re/runs/wpe-depth-e8a1: top h 879 = y 129).",
    "Seams (CAMPAIGN §4.1 join chunks, §12.2 6-3 'pillar chunk at the seam'): every join of two sources is covered by a spire pier (the brick jamb of the E7a0 arch, E7a0 1760-1792, palette row 27 lifted; a full-height foreground pillar) in the storm palette; every other join is a mirror join.",
    "Far layer: one per section; 6-1 the E1a2 skyline, 6-2 none (the E1a1 hall is opaque and has no scroll3), 6-3/6-4 one E6a0 span, 6-5 E8a2, 6-6 E8a1; changes sit under a pier.",
    "The Crown Engine is a boss sprite (WP-C bake from E8a3), never stage art. The spillway gate and wheels are code-created props at the listed section x.",
    "Section casts (CAMPAIGN §4.4 'cast', merged over the chapter pool): lighter A/BOMB/KNIFE variants where the ROM-affine HP budget of the chapter's waves exceeded ENEMIES §2.6 by more than 15% (tests/campaign.cjs (8)); ratio now 1.139.",
    "Palette: storm-crown on every slice; the role ops (sky borrow from E4a0, water tint) are skipped without roles, so the skies take s3ops (darkened, 30% toward #6a4a9a) to read as storm."
  ],
